wifi: mt76: mt7615: count tx status reports in debugfs

Add a debugfs file, txs_stats, with counters of the tx status reports,
to find out how they map to what rate control is told:

- status flags: ACK, RTS and queue timeouts, block ack errors, A-MPDU,
  fixed rate, no transmission at all, and reports that reach mac80211
  without rate information
- the time from the newest rate set update to the first transmission,
  which decides the rate set a report is credited to
- whether the final rate at the last slot used is in the chosen rate
  set, only in the other one, in both or in neither
- the bandwidth a report gives for the bandwidth of that rate
- the transmission count and the last rate slot used

Writing to txs_stats_reset clears the counters. This is a measurement
aid only; nothing else changes.

--- a/mt7615/debugfs.c
+++ b/mt7615/debugfs.c
